page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","content":"Integrate Ambriel into Cursor IDE via MCP: call fraud, AML and KYB tools directly from your editor while building risk features."},"198":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#cursor","content":"Cursor"},"199":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#setup","content":"Setup"},"200":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Which tools are exposed?"},"201":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#example","content":"Example"},"202":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#faq","content":"FAQ"},"203":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"204":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#cursor","content":"You can integrate Ambriel into Cursor IDE via MCP in minutes using OAuth, with no API keys to manage. Once enabled, Cursor's AI can call fraud scoring, AML screening, KYB evaluation, and email, phone, IP, and BIN lookups directly from your editor while you build and review risk features."},"205":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#cursor","content":"title: Prerequisites"},"206":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#cursor","content":"You need a recent Cursor version with MCP Servers under Features, plus an Ambriel account with compliance API access. A browser is required for the one-time OAuth approval — after that the token persists across restarts."},"207":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#cursor","content":"The Cursor integration shines during implementation: validate a signup form against real risk data, generate fixtures from live lookups, or ask the agent to wire a screening step into onboarding. Tools run in context, so Cursor sees your code and the response together."},"208":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#setup","content":"Go to Cursor Settings → Features → MCP Servers."},"209":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#setup","content":"Click Add New MCP Server and enter:"},"210":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#setup","content":"Name: ambriel"},"211":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#setup","content":"Type: url"},"212":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#setup","content":"URL: https://mcp.ambriel.io/compliance"},"213":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#setup","content":"Prefer JSON config? Paste this into your mcp.json:"},"214":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#setup","content":"Save and confirm the server shows a green connected status."},"215":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#setup","content":"After adding the server, Cursor will prompt you to authorize the connection. A browser window will open — log in with your Ambriel credentials and approve the access request."},"216":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#setup","content":"Return to Cursor and verify the Ambriel tools appear in the MCP tool list. If the browser flow stalls, copy the redirect URL into your default browser manually."},"217":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#setup","content":"The Ambriel tools are now available to Cursor's AI. Try asking:"},"218":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#setup","content":"\"Check if this email is risky\""},"219":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#setup","content":"\"Screen this company for PEP status\""},"220":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-23","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#setup","content":"\"Look up this phone number\""},"221":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-24","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#setup","content":"In Agent mode, try a code-aware prompt: \"Add an AML screen to this signup handler and test it with a sanctioned name.\" Cursor will call Ambriel, show the result, and propose the diff."},"222":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-25","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#setup","content":"Cursor's AI will automatically use the MCP tools when relevant to your code. For example, if you're reviewing a user registration flow, it can check the email and phone in real time."},"223":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-26","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Cursor's agent picks tools from intent, but you can also name them explicitly in prompts for deterministic behavior."},"224":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-27","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Tool"},"225":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-28","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"What it does"},"226":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-29","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"fraud-score"},"227":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-30","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Scores transactions and onboarding attempts inline"},"228":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-31","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"aml-screen"},"229":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-32","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Screens names and companies against sanctions and PEP lists"},"230":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-33","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"email-lookup"},"231":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-34","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Flags disposable, invalid, or breached emails during signup"},"232":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-35","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"phone-lookup"},"233":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Validates phone input with carrier and reachability signals"},"234":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"ip-lookup"},"235":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Detects proxies, VPNs, and geo mismatches at request time"},"236":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"kyb-evaluate"},"237":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Pulls company risk context while building KYB review UI"},"238":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"bin-lookup"},"239":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-42","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Resolves card BINs when testing checkout logic"},"240":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-43","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Scope-heavy repos benefit from naming the tool: \"Use ip-lookup on this request IP and decide whether to step up auth.\""},"241":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-44","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#example","content":"Ask Cursor to combine code and live data in one turn — generating a fixture from a real lookup or adding retry logic around a screening call."},"242":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-45","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#faq","content":"Name the tool explicitly, for example: \"Use ambriel email-lookup on test@example.com and quote the verdict.\" Agent mode with MCP tools enabled is more reliable than Ask mode."},"243":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-46","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#faq","content":"Keep MCP Servers enabled under Features, allow network access to mcp.ambriel.io, and update to the latest release. If tools disappear after an update, remove and re-add the server, then re-authorize once."},"244":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-47","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#faq","content":"Yes. Cursor supports global mcp.json and project-level .cursor/mcp.json. Use project config to pin the compliance URL per repo and isolate personal experiments."},"245":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-48","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#faq","content":"No. Only the tool arguments you approve (such as an email or IP) go to Ambriel. Review the tool-call preview before accepting, especially in repos with secrets or customer PII."},"246":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"page","content":"Devin","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin"},"247":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","content":"Connect Ambriel to Devin AI via MCP: let your autonomous engineer query fraud scores and screening results while it codes."},"248":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#devin","content":"Devin"},"249":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"Setup"},"250":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Which tools are exposed?"},"251":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#example","content":"Example"},"252":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#faq","content":"FAQ"},"253":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"254":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#devin","content":"You can connect Ambriel to Devin AI via MCP with a single config block and OAuth, no API keys needed. Once linked, your autonomous engineer can query fraud scores, run AML screens, and enrich emails, phones, IPs, and BINs while it implements and tests risk workflows on its own."},"255":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#devin","content":"title: Prerequisites"},"256":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#devin","content":"You need a Devin workspace with MCP support and permission to edit .devin/config.json, plus an Ambriel account with compliance API access. Keep a browser handy for the first-run OAuth approval that authorizes Devin's tool calls."},"257":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#devin","content":"Devin suits tasks spanning many steps: scaffolding a screening service, backfilling KYB checks, or adding fraud gates to checkout. With Ambriel tools available, Devin grounds decisions in live risk data and cites real responses in its PR summary."},"258":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"Devin uses a .devin/config.json configuration file in your project root. Create or edit the file."},"259":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"Add the following configuration with the URL format:"},"260":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"Commit the file so every Devin session in that repo inherits the connector. Use a global Devin MCP setting instead if you want Ambriel available across all repositories."},"261":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"When you first use an Ambriel tool, Devin will open a browser window for OAuth authentication. Sign in with your Ambriel credentials and authorize the connection."},"262":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"Approve the scopes once. Devin persists the session token, so subsequent tasks reuse it without interrupting the run."},"263":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"The Ambriel tools are now available to Devin."},"264":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"Assign a concrete task to verify: \"Add AML screening to the vendor onboarding endpoint, test it with two sample companies, and report the verdicts.\" Watch the session log for aml-screen and kyb-evaluate calls before it opens the PR."},"265":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"You can configure MCP servers globally or per-session in Devin's settings panel."},"266":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Devin sees the full compliance surface and can chain tools across long-running plans without further prompting."},"267":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Tool"},"268":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"What it does"},"269":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"fraud-score"},"270":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-23","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Scores transactions Devin creates during testing"},"271":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-24","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"aml-screen"},"272":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-25","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Screens people and vendors in bulk onboarding jobs"},"273":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-26","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"email-lookup"},"274":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-27","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Validates test and seed emails for deliverability"},"275":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-28","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"phone-lookup"},"276":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-29","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Checks phone fixtures for validity and carrier data"},"277":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-30","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"ip-lookup"},"278":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-31","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Flags proxy or datacenter IPs in abuse-handling code"},"279":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-32","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"kyb-evaluate"},"280":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-33","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Fetches company risk profiles for review queues"},"281":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-34","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"bin-lookup"},"282":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-35","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Resolves BINs while building payment validations"},"283":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"For audits, ask Devin to log every verdict: \"Record each screening result with entity, tool, and timestamp in the PR description.\""},"284":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#example","content":"Give Devin an outcome, not just a function — for example, backfilling screens for existing merchants or adding a blocklist check with passing tests. It will plan, call Ambriel, iterate, and summarize evidence."},"285":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#example","content":"Review the session transcript for tool inputs before merging. Devin's autonomy is powerful, but screening thresholds and block decisions should still get human approval."},"286":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#faq","content":"Use OAuth, not your password: Devin opens an Ambriel authorization page for scoped access. For shared machines, create a dedicated service identity so Devin's calls are attributed separately."},"287":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#faq","content":"Use .devin/config.json when the whole team needs compliance checks in that codebase, and global config for personal experiments. Repo config wins on conflicts."},"288":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#faq","content":"Instruct it explicitly: \"Only use synthetic fixtures, never real customer PII, and mock Ambriel in unit tests.\" Reserve live calls for integration sessions with approved test entities."},"289":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-42","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#faq","content":"Yes. Ask for batched kyb-evaluate calls with retries and a CSV summary of verdicts. Start with a small batch to validate match logic, then scale up."},"290":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"page","content":"AI Agents & MCP","url":"/docs/ui/agents"},"291":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents","content":"Connect Ambriel to Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Windsurf and more via MCP: query live risk data from your favorite AI assistant."},"292":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents#what-is-mcp","content":"What is MCP?"},"293":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents#authentication","content":"Authentication"},"294":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents#available-agents","content":"Available Agents"},"295":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Which tools are exposed?"},"296":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents#quick-start","content":"Quick Start"},"297":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents#faq","content":"FAQ"},"298":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"299":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents","content":"You can connect Ambriel to Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Devin, and other assistants via one MCP server at https://mcp.ambriel.io/compliance. Authenticate once with OAuth and your agent can immediately query live fraud scores, AML screens, KYB profiles, and reputation lookups without manual API keys."},"300":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents","content":"title: Prerequisites"},"301":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents","content":"You need an Ambriel account with compliance API access and an MCP-capable client (Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Devin, or Windsurf). Setup clicks differ; the server URL is the same."},"302":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents","content":"Ambriel's MCP server lets agents call the API directly — fraud scores, entity screens, email/phone/IP checks, and KYB evaluations from inside your AI tool."},"303":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#what-is-mcp","content":"The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is an open standard that connects AI models with external tools and data sources. Ambriel's MCP server acts as a bridge, giving your AI agent access to the full Ambriel API surface."},"304":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#what-is-mcp","content":"Instead of copying data between dashboard and assistant, the model calls Ambriel tools mid-conversation and reasons over fresh JSON. You get grounded answers — \"this IP is a datacenter proxy\" — rather than guesses from training data."},"305":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#authentication","content":"Ambriel's MCP server uses OAuth for authentication. When you first connect, your agent opens a browser window for Ambriel login and authorization. No manual API key management is needed."},"306":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#authentication","content":"Tokens are scoped to your user and org, so agents inherit exactly your permissions. Revoking access in Ambriel disconnects every agent session at once."},"307":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#available-agents","content":"Claude and ChatGPT suit investigations; Cursor and Devin suit builders wiring screening into code."},"308":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Every agent gets the same governed compliance toolset through the single MCP endpoint. The model selects tools from your wording, or you can name one explicitly."},"309":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Tool"},"310":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"What it does"},"311":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"fraud-score"},"312":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Scores transactions and customers with risk reasons"},"313":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"aml-screen"},"314":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-23","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Screens people and companies against sanctions and PEP lists"},"315":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-24","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"email-lookup"},"316":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-25","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Checks email validity, deliverability, and breach history"},"317":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-26","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"phone-lookup"},"318":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-27","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Validates phones with carrier and reachability signals"},"319":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-28","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"ip-lookup"},"320":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-29","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Enriches IPs with geo, ASN, and proxy/VPN detection"},"321":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-30","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"kyb-evaluate"},"322":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-31","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Builds company risk profiles for KYB reviews"},"323":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-32","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"bin-lookup"},"324":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-33","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Resolves card BINs to issuer, scheme, and country"},"325":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-34","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#quick-start","content":"One URL for all agents — OAuth handles authentication, no API key needed."},"326":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-35","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#quick-start","content":"One endpoint for every client:"},"327":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#quick-start","content":"Paste the URL into your client's MCP settings — see the agent guides above for exact clicks."},"328":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#quick-start","content":"A browser window opens on first use. Sign in, approve scopes, and return. The hammer or tools indicator confirms tools are live."},"329":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#quick-start","content":"Try: \"Screen John Doe from Germany against AML watchlists.\" A grounded answer quoting tool output means you are connected."},"330":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#quick-start","content":"When you add the MCP server, your AI agent will open a browser to authorize with Ambriel. Accept the prompt, and the connection is established. Your session is persisted for subsequent uses."},"331":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#faq","content":"Claude/ChatGPT suit investigations, Cursor suits live coding, Devin suits autonomous builds — same tools underneath."},"332":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#faq","content":"Use https://mcp.ambriel.io/compliance in production. It exposes fraud, AML, KYB, and all lookup tools behind OAuth."},"333":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-42","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#faq","content":"Yes — every call is metered under your identity and logged. Start narrow, then scale up."},"334":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-43","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#faq","content":"Revoke the OAuth grant in Ambriel account settings to disconnect all sessions, or remove the connector inside the specific client."},"335":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"page","content":"Digital Footprint","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint"},"336":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","content":"See how Ambriel tracks devices, behavior and location signals to catch fake accounts and fraud before checkout completes."},"337":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#what-is-digital-footprint","content":"What is Digital Footprint?"},"338":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Signal categories"},"339":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#device-identification","content":"Device identification"},"340":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#device-safety-and-security-checks","content":"Device safety and security checks"},"341":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#email-phone-and-ip-reputation","content":"Email, phone, and IP reputation"},"342":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#real-time-location-tracking","content":"Real-time location tracking"},"343":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#network-and-connection-monitoring","content":"Network and connection monitoring"},"344":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#analyzing-software-hardware-environment-and-screen-data","content":"Analyzing software, hardware environment, and screen data"},"345":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#behavioral-and-environmental-analysis","content":"Behavioral and environmental analysis"},"346":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#geofencing-for-location-based-regulation-compliance-igaming","content":"Geofencing for location-based regulation compliance (iGaming)"},"347":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#how-is-the-fingerprint-collected","content":"How is the fingerprint collected?"},"348":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#using-footprint-data-in-decisions","content":"Using footprint data in decisions"},"349":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#faq","content":"FAQ"},"350":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#what-is-digital-footprint","content":"Digital footprint is the trail of data users leave when interacting with your product — device attributes, network details, location consistency, contact-data history, and behavior patterns. Ambriel's digital footprint capabilities turn that trail into fraud evidence by revealing patterns of online behavior, identifying suspicious activity, and verifying the authenticity of user profiles before money moves."},"351":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#what-is-digital-footprint","content":"In short: Ambriel links the device, network, contact details, and behavior of every session into one identity picture, so fakes stand out even when the name on the account looks legitimate. The signals feed the Scoring Engine and appear as evidence on each row of the Transactions queue."},"352":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#what-is-digital-footprint","content":"type: info"},"353":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#what-is-digital-footprint","content":"Footprint signals are enrichment, not verdicts. One red flag rarely decides a transaction — combine signals in scoring rules so genuine users on odd networks are not blocked by a single anomaly."},"354":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Signal"},"355":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"What it catches"},"356":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Device identification"},"357":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Multi-accounting rings and returning banned users by linking sessions across identities on the same hardware"},"358":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Device safety and security checks"},"359":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-23","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Rooted or jailbroken phones, emulators, and tampered environments used to spoof legitimate devices"},"360":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-24","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Email reputation and breach exposure"},"361":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-25","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Fake and disposable addresses, plus credentials already leaked in breaches and reused by account-takeover crews"},"362":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-26","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Phone carrier and line-type intelligence"},"363":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-27","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"VoIP burners, invalid ranges, and recently ported numbers typical of one-time abuse accounts"},"364":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-28","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"IP reputation and network analysis"},"365":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-29","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Anonymous proxies, VPN exit nodes, Tor, hosting ranges, and botnets masking the attacker's true origin"},"366":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-30","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Real-time location tracking"},"367":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-31","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Impossible travel, billing-country mismatch, and geolocation spoofing at checkout or login"},"368":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-32","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Software, hardware, and screen analysis"},"369":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-33","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Headless browsers, mismatched screen and OS fingerprints, and automation frameworks pretending to be human"},"370":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-34","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Behavioral and environmental analysis"},"371":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-35","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Bot-speed form fills, copy-paste credential stuffing, and interaction patterns no human repeats at scale"},"372":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Geofencing for regulated markets"},"373":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Out-of-jurisdiction play and GPS manipulation for iGaming compliance and location-gated promotions"},"374":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#device-identification","content":"Track unique devices across web and mobile platforms, linking activity across multiple sessions. When five \"different\" customers share one fingerprint, you are looking at one operator, not five buyers."},"375":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#device-safety-and-security-checks","content":"Verify the security status of a device before allowing access to your platform. This ensures that your users are legitimate and not using compromised devices such as rooted phones or emulated environments."},"376":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#email-phone-and-ip-reputation","content":"These three contact-and-network signals validate the identity anchors of an account. Disposable emails, fresh domains with no history, VoIP numbers with no tenure, and datacenter IPs each add risk weight — and together they reliably separate throwaway fraud accounts from established genuine users."},"377":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#real-time-location-tracking","content":"Track the real-time location of users, allowing you to ensure that their geolocation matches expected behavior. This is essential for spotting suspicious access attempts or potential fraud such as logins from two countries minutes apart."},"378":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-42","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#network-and-connection-monitoring","content":"Monitor the user's network and connection details to identify suspicious activity and prevent fraud, from ASN reputation to proxy and tunnel detection."},"379":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-43","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#analyzing-software-hardware-environment-and-screen-data","content":"Verify the authenticity of devices and detect potential tampering or manipulation by analyzing the software, hardware, and screen data of each user device — the inconsistencies automation leaves behind."},"380":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-44","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#behavioral-and-environmental-analysis","content":"Monitor user behavior in real time and flag deviations that could indicate fraudulent or automated activities, such as inhuman input speed or perfectly repeated interaction sequences."},"381":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-45","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#geofencing-for-location-based-regulation-compliance-igaming","content":"Integrate with real-time location tracking to validate that transactions align with local regulations, ensuring compliance while blocking suspicious attempts to manipulate location data."},"382":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-46","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#how-is-the-fingerprint-collected","content":"Collection starts with the lightweight JavaScript agent embedded on your pages — it captures device attributes, browser and screen characteristics, and behavioral telemetry during the session and attaches them to the scoring request. Follow the JS agent setup guide to install the snippet, verify events are flowing, and confirm fingerprints appear on test transactions."},"383":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-47","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#how-is-the-fingerprint-collected","content":"Native mobile SDKs provide the equivalent telemetry for iOS and Android, while server-side lookup APIs enrich email, phone, and IP fields that never touch the frontend. All three paths converge: the agent and SDKs supply what only the client can observe, the lookups add historical reputation, and the Fraud API merges everything into one footprint per transaction."},"384":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-48","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#how-is-the-fingerprint-collected","content":"type: warning"},"385":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-49","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#how-is-the-fingerprint-collected","content":"Load the agent on every page where risk matters — signup, login, and checkout — not just the payment step. Fraudsters probe early; a fingerprint captured at account creation links the later fraudulent purchase back to the same device."},"386":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-50","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#using-footprint-data-in-decisions","content":"Reference footprint fields directly in scoring rules: block datacenter IPs on high-value orders, route disposable-email signups to review, or step up authentication when device and billing country diverge. Each row in the Transactions queue shows the footprint behind its score, so reviewers see the same evidence the rules used."},"387":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-51","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#faq","content":"In most regions, device and behavior collection counts as processing that needs disclosure and often consent. Publish it in your privacy policy, wire the agent to your consent manager, and confirm the legal basis with counsel before launch."},"388":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-52","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#faq","content":"You still get a decision. The footprint is thinner — fewer device and behavior attributes — so rules should treat missing telemetry as a mild risk factor rather than an automatic block, and lean on server-side email, phone, and IP lookups."},"389":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-53","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#faq","content":"Sophisticated attackers can rotate some attributes, but rarely all of them at once across device, network, behavior, and contact history. Layered signals plus velocity tracking make large-scale evasion expensive, which is what stops most operations."},"390":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-54","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#faq","content":"Install the agent in staging per the setup guide, run a test signup and checkout, then open the matching rows in the review queue and confirm device, IP, and behavior evidence is attached before promoting to production."},"391":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"page","content":"Fraud Prevention","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention"},"392":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","content":"Stop fraud before it costs you: real-time scoring, device intelligence and rule automation for transactions across every industry."},"393":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#fraud-scoring-api","content":"Fraud scoring API"},"394":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#digital-footprint","content":"Digital footprint"},"395":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#device-intelligence","content":"Device intelligence"},"396":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#scoring-engine-and-rules","content":"Scoring engine and rules"},"397":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#transaction-review-queue","content":"Transaction review queue"},"398":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#aml-and-compliance","content":"AML and compliance"},"399":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Which product do I need?"},"400":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#products","content":"Products"},"401":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#faq","content":"FAQ"},"402":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","content":"Ambriel is a comprehensive suite of fraud prevention and compliance solutions tailored for financial services, fintechs, iGaming operators, e-commerce platforms, retailers, and other digital businesses seeking effective risk management tools."},"403":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","content":"Start here if you are new: pick the product area that matches your problem below, then follow its guide to integrate and go live. You can adopt one tool for a targeted need or combine them into a layered defense across every transaction."},"404":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#fraud-scoring-api","content":"The Fraud API is Ambriel's primary real-time decisioning endpoint. You submit transaction, customer, and session data in a single request and receive an enriched response with risk scores, triggered rules, and a recommended decision in milliseconds."},"405":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#fraud-scoring-api","content":"Use it when you need a synchronous approve-or-block answer at checkout, signup, or login. It consolidates digital footprinting, decisioning, and risk scoring into one streamlined response, so your backend makes one call instead of orchestrating five vendors."},"406":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#digital-footprint","content":"Digital Footprint reveals who is really behind a session by analyzing online behavior, device identity, location consistency, and contact-data reputation. The Email, Phone, and IP signals expose disposable addresses, breached credentials, VoIP burner numbers, and anonymized or high-risk networks before money moves."},"407":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#digital-footprint","content":"Use it when fake accounts, friendly-fraud chargebacks, or promo abuse keep slipping through. Read the Digital Footprint guide for the full signal catalog and collection setup."},"408":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#device-intelligence","content":"Device Intelligence tracks device attributes, behavioral biometrics, and interaction patterns across web and mobile sessions. By fingerprinting configurations, browser settings, and usage behavior, it exposes bots, device spoofing, emulators, and multi-accounting rings that rotate identities but reuse hardware."},"409":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#device-intelligence","content":"Use it when one attacker controls many accounts, or when automated credential stuffing and card testing spike. Pair it with velocity rules in the scoring engine to throttle repeat offenders automatically."},"410":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#scoring-engine-and-rules","content":"The Scoring Engine turns your risk policy into executable logic: custom rules over IP, customer, phone, email, BIN, and transaction attributes, combined with AND/OR/NOT operators into Approve, Review, and Reject outcomes. Analysts tune thresholds and actions without shipping code."},"411":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#scoring-engine-and-rules","content":"Use it when static vendor scores do not match your risk appetite, or when you need different policies per market, product line, or payment method. See Scoring Engine for rule types, score bands, and worked examples."},"412":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#transaction-review-queue","content":"The Transactions queue is where analysts work the output of the engine: every scored event with its decision, score, rule trace, and evidence panel in one searchable list. Triage review-band traffic, approve or overturn decisions with a recorded audit trail, and export case files for disputes and regulators."},"413":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#transaction-review-queue","content":"Use it when manual review is part of your flow, or when chargebacks demand evidence fast. The Transactions guide walks through filters, risk bands, and the daily triage routine."},"414":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#aml-and-compliance","content":"Ambriel's AML screening and monitoring tools simplify regulatory adherence while strengthening fraud detection. Watchlist and sanctions checks run alongside fraud scoring, so a single transaction view covers both financial-crime risk and compliance exposure."},"415":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-23","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#aml-and-compliance","content":"Use it when onboarding customers under KYC obligations, or when ongoing monitoring must flag sanctioned entities and suspicious patterns. These tools integrate with the Fraud API for a holistic prevention posture."},"416":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-24","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Symptom"},"417":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-25","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Product"},"418":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-26","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Start with"},"419":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-27","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Fake signups and disposable emails"},"420":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-28","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Digital Footprint"},"421":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-29","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Digital Footprint"},"422":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-30","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"One device running many accounts"},"423":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-31","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Device Intelligence"},"424":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-32","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Digital Footprint"},"425":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-33","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Need a real-time approve-or-block answer"},"426":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-34","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Fraud scoring API"},"427":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-35","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Scoring Engine"},"428":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Vendor scores don't match our risk appetite"},"429":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Scoring Engine and rules"},"430":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Scoring Engine"},"431":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Review team drowning in manual checks"},"432":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Transaction review queue"},"433":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Transactions"},"434":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-42","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Chargebacks need evidence packs"},"435":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-43","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Transaction review queue"},"436":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-44","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Transactions"},"437":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-45","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Sanctions and watchlist obligations"},"438":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-46","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"AML and compliance"},"439":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-47","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"AML Compliance"},"440":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-48","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"type: info"},"441":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-49","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Most teams combine at least three layers: footprint signals for enrichment, scoring rules for automated decisions, and the review queue for human oversight. Start with scoring plus one signal source, then add layers as false positives and fraud losses dictate."},"442":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-50","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#faq","content":"Individually. Each product area works standalone — for example, lookup APIs for signup validation only — and they compose into a full risk stack when you are ready. Start with your most painful fraud vector and expand from there."},"443":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-51","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#faq","content":"The Fraud API plus the JavaScript agent gives you scored transactions with device and behavior signals in days. Lookup APIs for email, phone, and IP can ship even faster since they need no frontend changes."},"444":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-52","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#faq","content":"No — it focuses it. Automated rules clear the obvious approves and rejects so analysts spend time only on ambiguous review-band cases, with full evidence and an audit trail for every decision."},"445":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"page","content":"Scoring Engine","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine"},"446":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","content":"Learn how Ambriel scores each transaction with custom rules, score bands and decision states that approve, review or reject risk."},"447":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#scoring-engine","content":"Scoring Engine"},"448":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#how-is-the-score-calculated","content":"How is the score calculated?"},"449":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Rule Types"},"450":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#conditions","content":"Conditions"},"451":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#actions","content":"Actions"},"452":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"What do score bands mean?"},"453":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#how-do-rules-interact-with-scores","content":"How do rules interact with scores?"},"454":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Examples"},"455":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#faq","content":"FAQ"},"456":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#scoring-engine","content":"The Scoring Engine evaluates every transaction against your custom rules and produces a 0–100 risk score plus an Approve, Review, or Reject decision. Rules inspect IP, customer, phone, email, BIN, and transaction attributes, combine with logical operators, and the highest-priority match sets the outcome reviewers see in the queue."},"457":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#scoring-engine","content":"The Scoring Engine works by allowing you to define a set of rules that are evaluated for each transaction. Each rule has a set of conditions that are evaluated, and if all conditions are true, the rule is triggered. The triggered rule can then perform an action, such as setting a score, setting a state (Approve, Reject, Review), or adding a value to a list."},"458":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#how-is-the-score-calculated","content":"Each transaction runs through your rule set in priority order. Every rule whose conditions all evaluate to true fires and applies its action — setting or adjusting the score, assigning a decision state, or tagging the transaction via a list. When several rules match, the engine resolves them by priority so the most specific or most severe rule wins, and the full trace of fired rules is stored as evidence on the Transactions row."},"459":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#how-is-the-score-calculated","content":"type: info"},"460":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#how-is-the-score-calculated","content":"Scores are deterministic: the same transaction data against the same rule set always yields the same score. That makes rule changes testable — clone a rule, adjust it, and replay recent traffic before promoting."},"461":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"The following rule types are available:"},"462":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Rule Type"},"463":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Description"},"464":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"IP Rule"},"465":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Evaluates the IP address of the transaction."},"466":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Customer Rule"},"467":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Evaluates the customer information associated with the transaction."},"468":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","ur