"content":"Operator"},"478":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-32","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#conditions","content":"Description"},"479":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-33","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#conditions","content":"AND"},"480":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-34","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#conditions","content":"Evaluates to true if all conditions are true."},"481":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-35","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#conditions","content":"OR"},"482":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#conditions","content":"Evaluates to true if any condition is true."},"483":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#conditions","content":"NOT"},"484":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#conditions","content":"Evaluates to true if the condition is false."},"485":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#actions","content":"If a rule is triggered, the action associated with the rule is performed. The following actions are available:"},"486":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#actions","content":"Action"},"487":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#actions","content":"Description"},"488":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-42","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#actions","content":"Set Score"},"489":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-43","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#actions","content":"Sets the score of the transaction to a specified value."},"490":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-44","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#actions","content":"Set State"},"491":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-45","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#actions","content":"Sets the state of the transaction to a specified value (Approve, Reject, Review)."},"492":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-46","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#actions","content":"Add to List"},"493":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-47","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#actions","content":"Adds a value to a list associated with the transaction."},"494":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-48","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"The numeric score maps to a decision band that drives the default action. Configure the thresholds to match your risk appetite; the standard interpretation is:"},"495":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-49","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"Band"},"496":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-50","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"Score"},"497":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-51","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"Meaning"},"498":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-52","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"Default decision"},"499":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-53","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"Low risk"},"500":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-54","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"0–29"},"501":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-55","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"Signals look clean; no risk rules fired"},"502":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-56","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"Approve"},"503":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-57","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"Medium risk"},"504":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-58","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"30–69"},"505":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-59","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"Suspicious indicators present but not conclusive"},"506":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-60","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"Review"},"507":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-61","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"High risk"},"508":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-62","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"70–100"},"509":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-63","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"Strong fraud signals or a block rule matched"},"510":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-64","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"Reject"},"511":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-65","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"Bands shown in the Transactions queue use these same cutoffs, so what analysts triage matches what the engine decided. Start with the defaults, then shift boundaries after measuring false-positive and fraud-catch rates over a few weeks of live traffic."},"512":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-66","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#how-do-rules-interact-with-scores","content":"Rules and scores work as a pair: score actions position the transaction inside a band, while state actions can pin the decision regardless of the number. A rule that sets state Reject blocks the transaction even if no score action pushed it into the high band, and a Review state routes it to the manual queue for a human call. Priority ordering decides conflicts — place narrow, high-confidence block rules above broad informational ones so the severe outcome wins."},"513":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-67","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#how-do-rules-interact-with-scores","content":"Lists add memory across transactions: a rule can tag a device, email domain, or BIN the first time it looks suspicious, and later rules can check list membership to escalate repeat offenders. This is how single-event signals from the Digital Footprint become velocity and repeat-offender logic without custom code."},"514":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-68","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"The following example shows a rule that sets the score to 10 if the IP address of the transaction is from the United States and the transaction amount is greater than $100:"},"515":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-69","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Rule Name"},"516":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-70","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Rule Type"},"517":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-71","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Conditions"},"518":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-72","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Action"},"519":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-73","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"US High Amount"},"520":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-74","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"IP Rule"},"521":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-75","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"IP Address is from United States AND Amount > 100"},"522":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-76","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Set Score to 10"},"523":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-77","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"The following example shows a rule that sets the state to Review if the customer's email address is not verified and the transaction amount is greater than $50:"},"524":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-78","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Rule Name"},"525":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-79","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Rule Type"},"526":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-80","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Conditions"},"527":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-81","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Action"},"528":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-82","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Unverified Email"},"529":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-83","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Email Rule"},"530":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-84","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Email Address is not verified AND Amount > 50"},"531":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-85","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Set State to Review"},"532":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-86","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"The following example shows a rule that sets the score to 20 if the IP address of the transaction is not from the United States and the transaction amount is greater than $100 and the customer's phone number is not verified and the email address is not verified and the BIN is not from Visa:"},"533":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-87","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Rule Name"},"534":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-88","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Rule Type"},"535":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-89","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Conditions"},"536":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-90","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Action"},"537":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-91","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"High Amount and Unverified Information"},"538":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-92","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"IP Rule"},"539":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-93","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"IP Address is not from United States AND Amount > 100 AND Phone Number is not verified AND Email Address is not verified AND BIN is not Visa"},"540":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-94","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Set Score to 20"},"541":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-95","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#faq","content":"All matching rules fire and their trace is recorded, but priority order decides the final score and state. Put specific high-severity rules first so they override broader informational rules evaluated later."},"542":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-96","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#faq","content":"Use score actions for graduated risk that bands can route, and state actions for hard policy — things that must always block or always review. Combining them lets the number reflect risk while the state enforces policy."},"543":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-97","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#faq","content":"Duplicate the rule, adjust the copy, and check its matches against recent transactions before swapping it into production. Watch the review-queue volume and overturn rate afterward to confirm the change helped."},"544":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"page","content":"Transactions","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions"},"545":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","content":"Track every scored transaction in Ambriel: filter by risk level, review signals and decisions, then export cases for audit trails."},"546":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#transactions","content":"Transactions"},"547":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#what-the-page-shows","content":"What the page shows"},"548":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Filtering transactions"},"549":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"Risk-band meanings"},"550":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#triaging-the-review-queue","content":"Triaging the review queue"},"551":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#sort-by-score-filter-to-review","content":"Sort by score, filter to Review"},"552":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#open-the-evidence-panel","content":"Open the evidence panel"},"553":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#decide-approve-reject-or-escalate","content":"Decide: approve, reject, or escalate"},"554":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#feed-the-outcome-back-into-rules","content":"Feed the outcome back into rules"},"555":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#export-and-audit-trail","content":"Export and audit trail"},"556":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#faq","content":"FAQ"},"557":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#transactions","content":"The Transactions page is your operational queue for every scored payment, signup, and login: each row shows the final decision, the risk score, and the signals behind it. Use it to triage review-band traffic daily, investigate individual cases with full evidence, and export audit-ready records for compliance."},"558":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#what-the-page-shows","content":"Each transaction row summarizes the full output of the Scoring Engine in one line: a unique transaction ID, timestamp, customer reference, amount and currency, payment method, the final decision state (Approve, Review, or Reject), and a numeric risk score from 0 to 100. Opening a row reveals the evidence panel — which rules fired, the Digital Footprint signals attached to the session (device, IP, email, phone), and the complete decision history including manual overrides and analyst notes."},"559":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#what-the-page-shows","content":"type: info"},"560":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#what-the-page-shows","content":"Decisions shown here are final: automated rule outcomes plus any manual review actions. When a reviewer changes a state, the original score and rule trace are preserved so audits always show what the engine decided first."},"561":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#what-the-page-shows","content":"Scores and states update in near real time as new events stream in, so the queue always reflects the latest posture. High-risk spikes — for example a burst of transactions from one device or IP range — surface at the top when you sort by score descending, which is the recommended default view for a morning triage shift."},"562":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Use filters to narrow the queue to the slice you need to work. Combine several filters at once — for instance, state Review plus score above 70 plus the last 24 hours — to build a focused review list."},"563":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Filter"},"564":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Use it to"},"565":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Decision state (Approve / Review / Reject)"},"566":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Work the manual queue: start with Review, then spot-check a sample of Approve and Reject"},"567":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Risk score range"},"568":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-23","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Focus on a band, e.g. 70–100 for urgent review or 30–69 for secondary checks"},"569":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-24","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Date and time range"},"570":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-25","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Reconstruct what happened during an incident window or reconcile a settlement period"},"571":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-26","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Customer reference or email"},"572":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-27","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Pull every transaction from one buyer for a dispute or chargeback investigation"},"573":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-28","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Amount range"},"574":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-29","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Isolate high-value exposure first when review capacity is limited"},"575":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-30","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Payment method / BIN"},"576":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-31","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Chase card-testing patterns tied to one issuer or card range"},"577":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-32","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"IP address or country"},"578":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-33","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Investigate geo-mismatch clusters or traffic from sanctioned regions"},"579":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-34","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Device ID"},"580":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-35","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Find multi-accounting rings reusing the same device across identities"},"581":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Rule name"},"582":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"See everything one rule caught to tune it or measure its precision"},"583":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#filtering-transactions","content":"Saved views keep your most-used combinations one click away. A typical team keeps three: \"Morning review\" (Review state, score 50+, last 24h), \"High value\" (amount above threshold, any state), and \"Disputes\" (filtered by customer on demand)."},"584":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"Scores map to decision bands that tell you how to act at a glance. Your exact thresholds are configurable in the Scoring Engine, but the default semantics are:"},"585":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"Band"},"586":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"Score"},"587":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-42","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"Meaning"},"588":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-43","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"Recommended action"},"589":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-44","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"Low risk"},"590":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-45","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"0–29"},"591":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-46","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"Signals look clean; no rule fired or only informational rules matched"},"592":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-47","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"Auto-approve; sample periodically for QA"},"593":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-48","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"Medium risk"},"594":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-49","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"30–69"},"595":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-50","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"One or more risk signals present but not conclusive"},"596":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-51","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"Route to manual review or step-up authentication"},"597":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-52","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"High risk"},"598":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-53","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"70–100"},"599":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-54","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"Strong fraud indicators or a Reject rule matched"},"600":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-55","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"Block or hold; review before any release"},"601":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-56","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#risk-band-meanings","content":"Bands are guidance, not verdicts: a low-score transaction with a fresh dispute still deserves a look, and a high-score transaction from a known VIP may warrant a call rather than an outright cancel."},"602":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-57","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#sort-by-score-filter-to-review","content":"Start each shift with decision state set to Review and sort by score descending. The riskiest cases needing a human decision sit at the top."},"603":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-58","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#open-the-evidence-panel","content":"Check which rules fired, the score breakdown, and the attached footprint: device reputation, IP geolocation versus billing country, email age and breach exposure, and phone carrier and line type."},"604":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-59","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#decide-approve-reject-or-escalate","content":"Approve genuine buyers, reject clear fraud, and escalate edge cases with a note. Every action records who decided, when, and why, so the next reviewer sees the full trail."},"605":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-60","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#feed-the-outcome-back-into-rules","content":"If a pattern repeats — the same BIN range, device, or email domain — take it to the Scoring Engine and tighten or add a rule so the next wave is handled automatically."},"606":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-61","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#export-and-audit-trail","content":"Select any set of transactions and export them to CSV for chargeback representment, internal reporting, or regulator requests. Each export includes the score, the decision state, the rules that fired, manual actions with analyst identities and timestamps, and the linked footprint evidence. Because the original automated decision is stored separately from later manual overrides, auditors can always distinguish what the engine decided from what a human changed — which is exactly what dispute and compliance reviews require."},"607":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-62","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#faq","content":"A Review state means a rule matched with a review action, or the score landed inside your configured review band. Open the evidence panel to see exactly which rule fired, then approve or reject manually — the decision and your note are recorded permanently."},"608":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-63","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#faq","content":"Yes. Reviewers with the right permissions can move a transaction between Approve, Review, and Reject. The change is appended to the decision history with who made it and when; the original engine decision is never overwritten."},"609":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-64","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#faq","content":"Retention follows your plan and regional settings. Transactions remain searchable and exportable for the full retention window, after which they are archived or purged according to your data policy."},"610":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions-65","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/transactions#faq","content":"Filter by the shared attribute — device ID, IP range, email domain, or BIN — across a wide date range, then sort by score. Linked rows sharing one device or network with different identities are the classic multi-accounting pattern; export the set as a case file and tighten a rule in the scoring engine."},"611":{"id":"/docs/ui/integration/bigcommerce","page_id":"/docs/ui/integration/bigcommerce","type":"page","content":"BigCommerce","url":"/docs/ui/integration/bigcommerce"},"612":{"id":"/docs/ui/integration/bigcommerce-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/integration/bigcommerce","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/integration/bigcommerce","content":"Connect Ambriel fraud prevention to BigCommerce: screen orders, verify buyers and block fraudulent payments with guided setup."},"613":{"id":"/docs/ui/integration/bigcommerce-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/integration/bigcommerce","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/integration/bigcommerce#in-progress","content":"In Progress"},"614":{"id":"/docs/ui/integration/bigcommerce-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/integration/bigcommerce","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/integration/bigcommerce#in-progress","content":"This page is currently being worked on and will be available soon."},"615":{"id":"/docs/ui/integration","page_id":"/docs/ui/integration","type":"page","content":"Getting Started","url":"/docs/ui/integration"},"616":{"id":"/docs/ui/integration-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/integration","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/integration","content":"Learn how to integrate Ambriel with your stack: REST APIs, the JavaScript agent and no-code plugins for major ecommerce platforms."},"617":{"id":"/docs/ui/integration-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/integration","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/integration#api-reference","content":"API Reference"},"618":{"id":"/docs/ui/integration-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/integration","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/integration#javascript-agent","content":"Javascript Agent"},"619":{"id":"/docs/ui/integration-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/integration","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/integration#e-commerce-plugins","content":"E-commerce Plugins"},"620":{"id":"/docs/ui/integration-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/integration","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/integration#rest-vs-js-agent-vs-plugin--which-should-you-choose","content":"REST vs JS agent vs plugin — which should you choose?"},"621":{"id":"/docs/ui/integration-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/integration","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/integration#whats-next","content":"What's Next?"},"622":{"id":"/docs/ui/integration-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/integration","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/integration","content":"Ambriel provides a range of integration options to help you get started quickly. Whether you're building a custom integration or using one of our pre-built plugins, we've got you covered."},"623":{"id":"/docs/ui/integration-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/integration","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/integration","content":"By integrating Ambriel with your existing services, you can create a seamless experience for integration. You can use Ambriel as if it were your own product, without needing to map any data or use new identifiers."},"624":{"id":"/docs/ui/integration-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/integration","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/integration","content":"You can use your own identifiers, such as customer_id, order_id, transaction_id, and more. This makes it easy to incorporate Ambriel into your existing workflows and processes, without having to make significant changes to your code or infrastructure."},"625":{"id":"/docs/ui/integration-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/integration","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/integration#api-reference","content":"If you're looking to build a custom integration, our API Reference is the perfect place to start. You'll find detailed documentation on all of our endpoints, including examples and code snippets to help you get started."},"626":{"id":"/docs/ui/integration-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/integration","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/integration#javascript-agent","content":"Our Javascript Agent provides a simple way to integrate Ambriel with your web application. You can use it to capture user data, track events, and trigger fraud checks."},"627":{