yment processors, crypto exchanges with graduated compliance requirements"},"849":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-119","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#best-use-cases","content":"Real scenario: A neobank uses this strategy to segment customers into risk tiers. Scores 0-20 get instant approval, 21-40 need document verification, 41+ require senior compliance sign-off."},"850":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-120","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#how-it-works-1","content":"This strategy uses only the single highest rule score as the final result. All other triggered rules are ignored for scoring purposes."},"851":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-121","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#how-it-works-1","content":"Philosophy: In compliance, one critical red flag (sanctions hit, fraud indicator, PEP exposure) should override everything else. A company can't be \"low risk\" just because it scored well on other criteria."},"852":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-122","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#real-world-example-1","content":"You're screening a corporate services provider. Three rules trigger:"},"853":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-123","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#real-world-example-1","content":"Rule Triggered"},"854":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-124","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#real-world-example-1","content":"Impact"},"855":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-125","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#real-world-example-1","content":"Likelihood"},"856":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-126","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#real-world-example-1","content":"Weight"},"857":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies