egies#strategy-combinations","content":"Onboarding: Cumulative Risk (for tiered approval workflows)"},"960":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-230","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#strategy-combinations","content":"Ongoing monitoring: Critical Risk (to catch emerging red flags)"},"961":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-231","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#strategy-combinations","content":"Portfolio reporting: Normalized Scoring (for executive dashboards)"},"962":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-232","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#1-set-realistic-thresholds","content":"Base your Low/Medium/High thresholds on operational capacity:"},"963":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-233","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#1-set-realistic-thresholds","content":"Low: Auto-approve or minimal review"},"964":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-234","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#1-set-realistic-thresholds","content":"Medium: Standard due diligence"},"965":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-235","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#1-set-realistic-thresholds","content":"High: Enhanced due diligence"},"966":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-236","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#1-set-realistic-thresholds","content":"Severe: Senior approval or reject"},"967":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-237","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#1-set-realistic-thresholds","content":"Example: If your team can handle 20 manual reviews daily, set thresholds so ~80% of companies fall in \"Low.\""},"968":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-238","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#2-calibrate-using-real-data","content":"Run your strategy on existing customers before going live:"},"969":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-239","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#3-document-your-choices","content":"Regulators expect you to explain your methodology:"},"970":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-240","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#3-document-your-choices","content":"Why this strategy?"},"971":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-241","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#3-document-your-choices","content":"How were thresholds determined?"},"972":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-242","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#3-document-your-choices","content":"What's your process for high-risk cases?"},"973":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-243","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#4-review-quarterly","content":"Risk landscapes change:"},"974":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-244","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#4-review-quarterly","content":"Are new fraud patterns emerging?"},"975":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-245","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#4-review-quarterly","content":"Did regulations update?"},"976":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-246","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#4-review-quarterly","content":"Is your rule set still relevant?"},"977":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-247","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#important-notes","content":"Strategies are flexible: Change anytime to match evolving needs Audit trail preserved: Past assessments keep their original scores and strategy for compliance records Rules run identically: Strategy only affects score calculation, not which rules trigger Full transparency: Every assessment shows exactly which rules fired and their individual scores"},"978":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-248","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#important-notes","content":"Compliance Note: All three strategies are acceptable under current AML/KYC regulations. Your choice should align with your documented risk appetite and be consistently applied. Changes to scoring strategy should be documented with business justification."},"979":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-249","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#need-help-deciding","content":"Common starting point: Use Cumulative Risk with moderate thresholds. It's the most versatile and easiest to explain to stakeholders."},"980":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-250","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#need-help-deciding","content":"Then adjust if:"},"981":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-251","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#need-help-deciding","content":"You're seeing too many false positives → Switch to Critical Risk or raise thresholds"},"982":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-252","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#need-help-deciding","content":"You need better portfolio analytics → Switch to Normalized Scoring"},"983":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-253","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#need-help-deciding","content":"Regulators want consistent metrics → Use Normalized with fixed max value"},"984":{"id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies-254","page_id":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/kyb/strategies#need-help-deciding","content":"Your Ambriel support team can analyze your rule set and recommend optimal strategy configuration based on your industry and use case."},"985":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"page","content":"AML Compliance","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance"},"986":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","content":"Meet AML obligations with Ambriel: sanctions and PEP screening, continuous monitoring and audit-ready case management in one place."},"987":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-is-aml-compliance-and-who-needs-it","content":"What is AML compliance, and who needs it?"},"988":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"What does Ambriel screen against?"},"989":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-real-time-screening-work","content":"How does real-time screening work?"},"990":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-continuous-monitoring-keep-you-covered-between-checks","content":"How does continuous monitoring keep you covered between checks?"},"991":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-ambriel-fit-with-the-rest-of-your-fraud-stack","content":"How does Ambriel fit with the rest of your fraud stack?"},"992":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#frequently-asked-questions","content":"Frequently asked questions"},"993":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-is-aml-compliance-and-who-needs-it","content":"Anti-Money Laundering (AML) compliance means knowing who your customers are, screening them against official watchlists, and watching for suspicious change over time. Any business that moves money or stores value — banks, fintechs, payment firms, crypto platforms, iGaming operators, marketplaces — is expected to run these checks and to prove they ran them."},"994":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-is-aml-compliance-and-who-needs-it","content":"Two frameworks shape almost every program. The Financial Action Task Force (FATF) sets the global standard with its recommendations on customer due diligence, sanctions screening, and Combating the Financing of Terrorism (CFT). In the European Union, the 5th and 6th Anti-Money Laundering Directives (AMLD5/6) turn those principles into hard obligations: verify customer identity, screen against sanctions and PEP lists, monitor on an ongoing basis, and keep records that auditors can inspect."},"995":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-is-aml-compliance-and-who-needs-it","content":"type: warning"},"996":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-is-aml-compliance-and-who-needs-it","content":"title: Screening is not optional under AMLD5/6"},"997":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-is-aml-compliance-and-who-needs-it","content":"Regulated firms must screen customers against sanctions lists and PEP databases at onboarding and re-screen them as lists change. Missing a listed person because a list updated after onboarding is still a breach."},"998":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Ambriel screens each entity against more than 120 sources across four list families. The table below summarizes what each family covers and why it matters for your risk decision."},"999":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"List family"},"1000":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"What it covers"},"1001":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Why you screen it"},"1002":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Sanctions lists"},"1003":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Individuals, companies, vessels, and organizations subject to economic sanctions (e.g. OFAC SDN, EU consolidated list, UN lists)"},"1004":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Doing business with a sanctioned party can be a criminal offence and trigger asset freezes"},"1005":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"PEP lists"},"1006":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Current and former holders of prominent public office, plus family members and close associates"},"1007":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"PEPs carry higher bribery and corruption exposure, so they need enhanced due diligence"},"1008":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Crime lists"},"1009":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-23","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Individuals and companies convicted of or wanted for fraud, money laundering, organized crime, and terrorism"},"1010":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-24","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Flags counterparties with a proven or suspected criminal footprint before you onboard them"},"1011":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-25","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Regulatory and watch lists"},"1012":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-26","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Enforcement actions, disqualified directors, adverse-media profiles, and law-enforcement watch data"},"1013":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-27","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Surfaces early-warning signals that do not appear on sanctions lists yet"},"1014":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-28","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Screening runs in real time at onboarding and repeats automatically while monitoring stays switched on, so a customer who becomes listed months later still generates an alert."},"1015":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-29","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-real-time-screening-work","content":"When you create an entity or call the AML screen endpoint, Ambriel normalizes the name and identifiers, searches the enabled lists, and returns scored matches instead of a blunt yes-or-no. Each hit carries a similarity score, the source list, and the matched profile, so analysts can tell a strong match from a coincidental name collision."},"1016":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-30","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-real-time-screening-work","content":"Check names, companies, and counterparties against sanctions, PEP, crime, and regulatory lists in seconds, at onboarding or inside any workflow."},"1017":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-31","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-real-time-screening-work","content":"Control which lists are searched and how strictly names must match in Search Configuration, balancing catch rate against false positives."},"1018":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-32","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-real-time-screening-work","content":"Route scored hits into review queues, clear false positives with a reason, and escalate genuine matches into case management with a full evidence trail."},"1019":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-33","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-continuous-monitoring-keep-you-covered-between-checks","content":"A one-time screen goes stale the day after it runs: lists are updated daily, PEPs leave and enter office, and clean customers can appear in enforcement actions. With monitoring enabled on an entity, Ambriel re-screens it every time the underlying lists refresh and pushes an alert when something changes — a new list appearance, a status change, or a fresh adverse-media profile."},"1020":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-34","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-continuous-monitoring-keep-you-covered-between-checks","content":"Because every search and every result is written to a secure, tamper-proof log retained for 5 years, each alert arrives with its history attached: what matched, when it matched, and what the analyst did about it. That log is your audit trail when a regulator asks how a flagged customer was handled."},"1021":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-35","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-ambriel-fit-with-the-rest-of-your-fraud-stack","content":"The AML API integrates seamlessly with the Fraud API, so a single customer view combines sanctions and PEP exposure with device intelligence, digital-footprint signals, and transaction risk scores. A typical wiring looks like this: score the transaction for fraud, screen the parties for AML exposure, and hold or step up anything that fails either check. Shared case management then keeps fraud and compliance decisions in one place instead of two disconnected queues."},"1022":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-ambriel-fit-with-the-rest-of-your-fraud-stack","content":"type: info"},"1023":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-ambriel-fit-with-the-rest-of-your-fraud-stack","content":"title: Where to go next"},"1024":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-ambriel-fit-with-the-rest-of-your-fraud-stack","content":"Model the people and companies you screen in Entities, run day-to-day checks from Screening and Monitoring, and calibrate precision in Search Configuration."},"1025":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#frequently-asked-questions","content":"Ambriel ingests list updates continuously and re-screens monitored entities as new data arrives — daily for fast-moving sanctions and PEP sources, on the schedule you configure for the rest. You never need to re-upload your customer base to pick up a new listing."},"1026":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#frequently-asked-questions","content":"The entity generates an alert with the matched profile, source list, and score. Your team triages it in the dashboard or via the API, then clears it with a documented reason or escalates it into a case — every step lands in the 5-year audit log."},"1027":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#frequently-asked-questions","content":"No. Ambriel automates the screening, monitoring, and record-keeping, but disposition decisions — clear, escalate, exit — stay with your compliance team and your risk policy. The platform's job is to make each decision fast, consistent, and provable."},"1028":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"page","content":"Entities","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities"},"1029":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","content":"Understand AML entities in Ambriel: how persons, companies and counterparties are modeled, screened and monitored continuously."},"1030":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#what-are-entities-in-aml-context","content":"What are Entities in AML Context?"},"1031":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Which entity types does Ambriel screen?"},"1032":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#politically-exposed-persons-pep","content":"Politically Exposed Persons (PEP)"},"1033":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#sanctions-lists","content":"Sanctions Lists"},"1034":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#crime-lists","content":"Crime Lists"},"1035":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#watch-lists","content":"Watch Lists"},"1036":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#why-are-entities-important-in-aml","content":"Why are Entities Important in AML?"},"1037":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-can-you-use-ambriels-entities-feature","content":"How Can You Use Ambriel's Entities Feature?"},"1038":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-to-create-an-entity","content":"How to create an Entity?"},"1039":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"Entity Fields"},"1040":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#what-are-entities-in-aml-context","content":"In the context of Anti-Money Laundering (AML), entities refer to individuals, companies, or organizations that are subject to AML regulations. These entities can be either natural persons (e.g. individuals) or legal persons (e.g. companies). Ambriel's AML solution scans over 120 sources and continuously improves to provide the most accurate and up-to-date information."},"1041":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"The four list families below cover different risk questions. Use the comparison table to decide which ones your policy needs enabled — most regulated firms enable all four and then tune precision in Search Configuration."},"1042":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Entity type"},"1043":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Who appears on it"},"1044":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Risk question it answers"},"1045":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Typical sources"},"1046":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Politically Exposed Persons (PEP)"},"1047":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Heads of state, ministers, MPs, judges, military leaders, state-company executives, plus family and close associates"},"1048":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Could this customer expose us to bribery or corruption proceeds?"},"1049":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Government gazettes, official PEP registers, commercial PEP databases"},"1050":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Sanctions lists"},"1051":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Individuals, companies, vessels, and organizations under economic or trade sanctions"},"1052":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-23","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Are we legally barred from doing business with this party?"},"1053":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-24","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"OFAC SDN, EU consolidated list, UN Security Council lists, national sanctions regimes"},"1054":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-25","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Crime lists"},"1055":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-26","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"People and companies convicted of or wanted for fraud, money laundering, organized crime, or terrorism"},"1056":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-27","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Does this counterparty have a proven or suspected criminal footprint?"},"1057":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-28","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"FBI Most Wanted, Interpol Red Notices, national conviction and enforcement records"},"1058":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-29","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Watch lists"},"1059":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-30","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"People and companies under surveillance or flagged in adverse media and enforcement actions"},"1060":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-31","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Is there an early-warning signal worth enhanced due diligence?"},"1061":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-32","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Law-enforcement bulletins, disqualified-director registers, adverse-media feeds"},"1062":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-33","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"type: info"},"1063":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-34","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"title: PEP screening includes associates"},"1064":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-35","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"A PEP hit is not an accusation — it means enhanced due diligence applies. Always check the listed role, country, dates in office, and any family or associate links before deciding."},"1065":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#politically-exposed-persons-pep","content":"PEPs are individuals who hold or have held prominent public offices, such as heads of state, government officials, politicians, or high-ranking military officers. PEPs are considered high-risk due to their potential exposure to corruption and bribery."},"1066":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#sanctions-lists","content":"Sanctions lists are compiled by governments and international organizations to identify individuals, companies, and organizations that are subject to economic sanctions. These sanctions can be imposed due to various reasons, such as supporting terrorism, human rights violations, or nuclear proliferation."},"1067":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#crime-lists","content":"Crime lists are databases of individuals and companies that have been convicted of or are suspected of committing crimes, such as fraud, money laundering, or organized crime."},"1068":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#watch-lists","content":"Watch lists are databases of individuals and companies that are under surveillance by law enforcement or other authorities. These lists are used to identify and monitor potential security threats, such as terrorists, organized crime groups, or individuals with a history of fraudulent activities. Watch lists can be used to flag suspicious transactions, prevent fraud, and protect against potential security threats."},"1069":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#why-are-entities-important-in-aml","content":"Entities play a crucial role in AML as they can be used to conceal illegal activities, such as money laundering and terrorist financing. Therefore, it is essential to identify and monitor entities to prevent illegal activities and ensure compliance with AML regulations."},"1070":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-can-you-use-ambriels-entities-feature","content":"Ambriel's Entities feature allows you to screen entities against PEP, sanctions, and crime lists in real-time. You can use this feature to:"},"1071":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-42","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-can-you-use-ambriels-entities-feature","content":"Verify the identity of customers and suppliers"},"1072":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-43","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-can-you-use-ambriels-entities-feature","content":"Check for potential AML risks"},"1073":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-44","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-can-you-use-ambriels-entities-feature","content":"Monitor transactions and activities"},"1074":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-45","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-can-you-use-ambriels-entities-feature","content":"Comply with AML regulations"},"1075":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-46","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-can-you-use-ambriels-entities-feature","content":"Once entities exist, keep them under continuous screening and monitoring so list updates surface as alerts instead of silent exposure."},"1076":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-47","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-to-create-an-entity","content":"Login to dashboard"},"1077":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-48","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-to-create-an-entity","content":"Go to Aml > Entities"},"1078":{"i